    <origin>Filed 2026-08-25. Design §5.1c: the same user-BU→container chain is repeated in at least seven places, plus the server-side archive path. Additionally `EntityCreationService.applyUserBuDefaults` stamps `sprk_containerid` onto secure projects today, which both defeats isolation and collided with provisioning's idempotency marker.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>The resolver from task 075 only matters if nothing bypasses it. Route every container-resolution call site through it, and stop the creation wizard from stamping a shared BU container onto secure projects.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE full-stack engineer. The deliverable is completeness — every path, proven, with no survivors.</role>

  <goal>No code decides which container to use except through task 075's resolver. The creation wizard no longer writes a BU container id onto secure records. Completeness is demonstrated, not asserted.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>THE CALL SITES, per design §5.1c and the workflow review — treat this list as a STARTING POINT and prove it complete, because prior counts in this project have been wrong every time:

Client (the user-BU → `businessunit.sprk_containerid` chain), at least seven:
- `CreateMatterWizard/main.tsx`
- `sprk_wizard_commands.js`
- `useWizardPageBootstrap.ts`
- `WorkspaceGrid.tsx`
- `SemanticSearchControl/NavigationService.ts`
- `EntityCreationService.applyUserBuDefaults`
- the five `*WizardDialog.tsx` callers
Canonical client resolver: `xrmProvider.getSpeContainerIdFromBusinessUnit`.

Server:
- `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` — the global `ArchiveContainerId` used by email/communication ingest. **This is the one easiest to forget**: no client, no wizard, no UI. If it is missed, secure attachments land in the shared archive.

⭐ **THE CREATE-PROJECT WIZARD DEFECT, traced end-to-end 2026-08-25 — read this before touching the wizard.** The ordering is already correct and does NOT need changing; the bug is a discarded return value, and it is roughly two lines.

Verified sequence inside `CreateProjectWizard.tsx` `onFinish`:

| # | Action | Line |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Resolve BU cascade defaults | 542-544 |
| 2 | `createProject(...)` — record created, `sprk_issecure` written | 561 |
| 3 | Work assignment / Event / Association | 575, 626, 665 |
| 4 | **Secure provisioning** (`provisionSecureProject`) | 688-698 |
| 5 | **File upload to SPE** | 708-712 |
| 6 | `createDocumentRecords` + RAG indexing | 721, 739 |

Two facts that together make this cheap to fix:
- **The "Add file(s)" step transfers ZERO bytes.** `FileUploadZone` validates and stages `File` objects in React state (`ADD_FILES` reducer); there is no fetch/XHR in it. The first byte moves on **Finish**.
- **Provisioning already runs BEFORE the upload** — step 4 precedes step 5 above.

So moving the Secure toggle earlier in the step order fixes nothing. **The actual defect**: `provisionSecureProject` RETURNS the new container id (`provisioningService.ts:46`), but `CreateProjectWizard.tsx:700-704` consumes only `success` and `errorMessage` — **the container id is discarded**, and `speContainerIdRef` is never refreshed. The upload at `:712` therefore uses `context.speContainerId`, resolved ONCE when the wizard opened (`CreateRecordWizard.tsx:221-227`) from `systemuser._businessunitid_value` → `businessunit.sprk_containerid`. Net effect: **a secure project's files are PUT into the shared BU container while the project row points at its own isolated one**, and `createDocumentRecords` (`:726`) stamps the BU container id onto the `sprk_document` rows.

The fix is to consume `provisionResult.data.speContainerId` at `:712` and `:726`. Two further notes: the wizard's own inline BU resolver at `src/solutions/CreateProjectWizard/src/main.tsx:88-98` is an **8th client call site** not in the list below; and a provisioning failure is non-fatal by design (`:700-704` only adds a success-screen warning), while an absent `authFetch`/`bffBaseUrl` skips provisioning with **no warning at all** — yet the success screen still claims (`:816-817`) the container was provisioned.

THE WIZARD WRITE-BACK, two related problems:
1. `EntityCreationService.applyUserBuDefaults` (`src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/EntityCreationService.ts`) applies `sprk_containerid` to secure projects. It must not.
2. `src/solutions/DocumentUploadWizard/sprk_subgrid_commands.js` overwrites `sprk_project.sprk_containerid` with the BU container when the field is not on the form. This defeats a correct resolver *after the fact* — a stamped project silently reverts to shared storage.

Both were implicated in the 409 provisioning regression, because `sprk_containerid` was shared state written by two different mechanisms. Provisioning now keys idempotency on ownership instead (task 021), but the write-back still corrupts the isolation marker.

WHY COMPLETENESS IS THE DELIVERABLE. Because SPE permissions are additive-only, a single missed call site means secure content sits in a shared container permanently, and no later permission change can retract it. Partial completion here is not partial credit — it is the same failure as no completion, for whichever path was missed.

INV-7: strategy 1's resolution stays client-side. Routing through the shared decision must respect that; consume 075's client half rather than moving BU resolution to the server.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/EntityCreationService.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/DocumentUploadWizard/sprk_subgrid_commands.js</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/pcf/SemanticSearchControl/SemanticSearchControl/services/NavigationService.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ — IncomingCommunicationProcessor archive path</file>
      <file role="reference">projects/unified-access-control-r2/design.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="build-plan">PROVE completeness. Grep for every container-id resolution and every `sprk_containerid` write across `src/client/**`, `src/solutions/**`, and `src/server/**`, and show the evidence. Prior route/site counts in this project were wrong every single time they were asserted rather than grepped.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT add an `issecure` test at individual call sites. Call sites ask the resolver; they do not make the decision. A call site containing the word `issecure` is a review failure.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Where a call site cannot resolve a container for a secure record, it must fail visibly — not silently proceed with a BU or archive container.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The creation wizard must not write `sprk_containerid` for secure records at all. Removing the write is preferred over conditioning it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Respect INV-7 — BU resolution stays client-side; consume 075's client half.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §12">PCF builds use `npm run build:prod`, never `npm run build`. Bump PCF versions in all four locations if any PCF ships.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/SECURE-DOCUMENTS-BUILD-PLAN.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/secure-project-workflow-review-2026-08-24.md</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Grep the full call-site inventory — every container resolution and every `sprk_containerid` write, client, solutions and server. Record it. Compare against the list in this task and report any additions found.</step>
    <step order="1">Route each site through 075's resolver.</step>
    <step order="2">Remove the wizard's `sprk_containerid` write for secure records (`EntityCreationService`), and fix the DocumentUploadWizard write-back that overwrites a stamped container.</step>
    <step order="3">Route the server-side ingest/archive path through the server half of the resolver.</step>
    <step order="4">Re-grep to prove no unrouted site remains. This is the acceptance evidence.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: creating a document against a secure record targets that record's container; against a non-secure record, the BU cascade is unchanged; the wizard no longer stamps secure records.</step>
    <step order="6">Build (`build:prod` for PCF), tests, publish size, CVE.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a call site resolves a container in a context where the owning record is not known — so the resolver cannot be asked — STOP and surface it. That is a modelling gap; guessing the container in an unknown context is exactly how shared-container co-mingling happened.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Task 075 provides the resolver; the client BU-resolution chain and the server archive path already exist.</existing>
    <extension>This is pure routing of existing call sites onto the new seam plus removal of a harmful write. No new component.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Task 075's resolver decides nothing if callers bypass it. Any missed site places secure content in a shared container permanently — SPE cannot retract it — and the wizard write-back would silently revert correctly-stamped projects to shared storage.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">All client container call sites routed through the resolver</output>
    <output type="code">Server ingest/archive path routed through the resolver</output>
    <output type="code">Wizard `sprk_containerid` write removed for secure records; DocumentUploadWizard write-back fixed</output>
    <output type="doc">notes — full call-site inventory with grep evidence, before and after</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Every container-resolution call site goes through task 075's resolver — proven by a re-grep showing no survivors.</criterion>
    <criterion>No call site contains its own `issecure` test.</criterion>
    <criterion>The creation wizard does not write `sprk_containerid` for secure records.</criterion>
    <criterion>The DocumentUploadWizard write-back can no longer overwrite a stamped secure container.</criterion>
    <criterion>The server-side ingest/archive path is routed (the easiest one to miss — verify explicitly).</criterion>
    <criterion>A document created against a secure record targets that record's own container, proven by a test.</criterion>
    <criterion>Non-secure behaviour is unchanged.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Completeness is the entire deliverable. Because SPE permissions are additive-only, one missed call site is a permanent isolation failure for whatever flows through it — there is no later fix. Grep, do not remember.</notes>
</task>
